---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

// Paste the YouTube video ID here and the Demo section appears automatically.
// https://youtu.be/ABC123xyz  ->  "ABC123xyz"
const youtubeId = 'qGvQYSoElsQ';

// Web edition of the catalogue (page-flip viewer).
// It initialises from its container's size and fails on wide, short boxes,
// so .book-embed below stays taller than ~1.4:1.
const catalogueUrl = 'https://transcendentcontact.vercel.app';

// NeurIPS 2026 Creative AI Track (Artwork), accepted.
const openreviewUrl = 'https://openreview.net/forum?id=hmFew1sLA2';
const neuripsUrl = 'https://neurips.cc/virtual/2026/loc/sydney/160645';
---

<Layout title="Transcendent Contact | Haeri Kim">
	<Nav />
	<main class="project-page">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="project-info reveal">
				<div class="project-heading">
					<h1>Transcendent Contact</h1>
					<p class="description">An AI-Fabricated Exhibition Catalogue Reframing Hallucination as Creative Capacity</p>
				</div>
				<aside class="wall-label" aria-label="NeurIPS 2026 acceptance">
					<span class="red-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
					<p class="wl-title">Transcendent Contact: Expanding Creative Agency Through AI Hallucination</p>
					<p class="wl-note">Accepted to the NeurIPS 2026 Creative AI Track as an Artwork.</p>
					<p class="wl-links">
						<a href={openreviewUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenReview entry</a>
						<a href={neuripsUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Conference listing</a>
					</p>
				</aside>
			</div>
			<div class="meta-grid reveal">
				<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Course</span><span class="meta-value">Design Project 2026</span></div>
				<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Team</span><span class="meta-value">4</span></div>
				<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Duration</span><span class="meta-value">3 months</span></div>
				<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Models</span><span class="meta-value">Gemini Imagen 3, Nano Banana Pro, Kling 3.0, GPT-5.5, Gemini Pro, Claude Sonnet 4.5</span></div>
			</div>
			<div class="project-content reveal">
				<p class="project-description">Transcendent Contact is a 182-page hardcover catalogue for a museum exhibition that never happened. Its palindromic title, SAW / WAS, divides the book in two. The first half presents artist biographies, captions, and installation photographs of eighteen works as genuine holdings, inviting real responses to unmade objects. Midway, it reveals the fiction and explores the history of human and machine hallucination. A closing archive documents production through chat logs, discarded visual errors, and categories used to group the works.</p>
				<h3 class="section-title">Catalogue</h3>
				<img src="/portfolio/images/courses/transcendent-contact-spreads.jpg" alt="Spreads from the Transcendent Contact catalogue" class="hero-image" />
				<p class="project-description">We treated AI hallucination as a design partner, not a defect. Generative models produced artworks, artist personas, technical specifications, and curatorial justifications. Unexpected gap-filling became creative alternatives rather than corrections. From these outputs, we derived nine potentials of hallucination and organized the exhibition around them: Comforting, Humanizing, Preparing, Immersing, Escaping, Bonding, Restoring, Redefining, and Inspiring.</p>
				<p class="project-description">Authorship remains deliberately unstable. Agency moves through generation, curation, encounter, revelation, and re-reading, circulating among creator, tool, curator, and reader. We argue that the unverified can function as reality, and that hallucination, understood as capacity rather than error, expands the conditions for creative work.</p>
				<div class="book-embed">
					<iframe
						src={catalogueUrl}
						title="Transcendent Contact catalogue, web edition"
						loading="lazy"
					></iframe>
				</div>
				<p class="embed-note">
					<a href={catalogueUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full-screen edition ↗</a>
				</p>
				{youtubeId && (
					<>
						<h3 class="section-title">Exhibition Introduction</h3>
						<div class="video-embed">
							<iframe
								src={`https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${youtubeId}`}
								title="Transcendent Contact exhibition introduction"
								loading="lazy"
								allow="accelerometer; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
								referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
								allowfullscreen
							></iframe>
						</div>
					</>
				)}
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
	.project-page { padding-top: 7rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; }
	.project-info { margin-bottom: 3rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 15.5rem; column-gap: 3.5rem; align-items: start; }
	/* Acceptance shown as a museum wall label hung beside the title, echoing the catalogue's museum documentation */
	.wall-label { position: relative; padding: 1.1rem 1.15rem 1rem; background: var(--color-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle); border-radius: 2px; box-shadow: 0 1px 0 var(--color-divider), 0 10px 18px -14px var(--color-shadow); }
	.wall-label p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text); }
	.project-page .wall-label .wl-title { font-family: var(--font); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: -0.01em; padding-right: 0.75rem; }
	.project-page .wall-label .wl-note { margin-top: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.76rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
	.project-page .wall-label .wl-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.3rem 1rem; margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.74rem; line-height: 1.4; }
	.wall-label a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--color-text-faint); text-underline-offset: 3px; transition: text-decoration-color 0.2s ease; }
	.wall-label a:hover { text-decoration-color: currentColor; }
	.wall-label a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent-cyan); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 1px; }
	/* Gallery red dot: the sticker that marks a work as taken */
	.red-dot { position: absolute; top: -0.45rem; right: -0.45rem; width: 1.05rem; height: 1.05rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-accent-red); box-shadow: inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.12), 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.18); animation: dot-press 0.45s cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.3) 1.1s both; }
	@keyframes dot-press { from { transform: scale(1.6) rotate(-20deg); opacity: 0; } to { transform: scale(1) rotate(0); opacity: 1; } }
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .red-dot { animation: none; } }
	.project-info h1 { font-family: var(--font); font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text); letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
	.description { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
	.meta-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1px; background-color: var(--color-border); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
	.meta-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 1.5rem; background-color: var(--color-bg); }
	.meta-label { font-family: var(--font); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
	.meta-value { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 500; }
	.project-content { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; }
	.hero-image { width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; }
	.video-embed { position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16/9; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--color-thumb); }
	.video-embed iframe { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; }
	.book-embed { position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 5/4; min-height: 520px; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); background: #FFFFFF; }
	.book-embed iframe { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; }
	.embed-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: -1rem; }
	.embed-note a { color: var(--color-text-secondary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
	.embed-note a:hover { color: var(--color-text); }
	.project-description { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
	.section-title { font-family: var(--font); font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-text); margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.project-info h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; }
		.project-info { grid-template-columns: 1fr; row-gap: 1.75rem; }
		.wall-label { max-width: 20rem; }
		.meta-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
		/* Narrow screens: the viewer drops to single-page, so give it portrait room */
		.book-embed { aspect-ratio: 3/4; min-height: 420px; }
	}
</style>
